    "changes": [
      {
        "area": "Device checkpoint write response",
        "semantics": "The authenticated POST persists and returns a strict same-run {runId,takenAt} receipt using the saved server timestamp instead of an empty 204. Existing admission row locks, owner/device/lease checks and secret masking remain."
      },
      {
        "area": "Daemon final checkpoint proof",
        "semantics": "Only a valid same-run persisted server receipt can certify the final archive. Old-server 204 remains accepted for transport compatibility but cannot certify a final archive. Server time avoids trusting device clock drift."
      },
      {
        "area": "Desktop computer grant authority",
        "semantics": "Execution is bound to authenticated run/device and, when present, the signed policy snapshot execution owner. A shared subscription payer is no longer incorrectly required to equal the execution/computer owner. Broker, lease, stopped/registered checks and policy verification remain. This is a real daemon authorization correction, not a claim of unchanged device authority semantics."
      },
      {
        "area": "Thread machine retirement",
        "semantics": "Only the existing successful provider acknowledgement update with the same owner/workspace/epoch/sandbox clears completed reconcileId/reconcileUntil claims, allowing immediate idempotent replay. Failure retry and unacknowledged creation are unchanged."
      },
      {
        "area": "Acceptance and test wiring",
        "semantics": "Adds persisted receipt, recovery/retirement, retention/idempotence, desktop owner and controlled PR-wait coverage in existing suites. package.json adds one archive test to test:workflow-wakes; our test:artifacts addition is independent."
      }
    ],
